<mujoco model="panda">
  <!-- Stage 2/3: vendored from google-deepmind/mujoco_menagerie's franka_emika_panda/
       panda_nohand.xml (Apache-2.0, see LICENSE in this directory), used as a static
       mujoco_model for mujoco_ros2_control (see panda_mujoco.ros2_control.xacro)
       instead of runtime URDF-to-MJCF conversion: robot_description_to_mjcf.sh has a
       reproducible bug where the last link in a converted joint chain always gets
       mis-placed and crashes ros2_control_node natively, confirmed across 3 different
       terminal links regardless of their content. This file sidesteps that tool
       entirely. Mass/inertia values here already match pinocchio_baseline/panda.urdf
       exactly (both sourced from the same real franka_description data).

       2026-07-22: despite the base file being the hand-less "nohand" variant, the hand
       and fingers ARE present here (added in an earlier session as welded, jointless mass
       to fix a gravity-compensation mismatch; given real joints/geometry this session for
       Stage 4 grasping — see the <body name="panda_hand"> comment below). Model name
       updated from "panda nohand" accordingly; some finger geometry (visual meshes,
       fingertip pad collision boxes) was additionally pulled from mujoco_menagerie's
       WITH-hand panda.xml, since panda_nohand.xml has none of it.

       Changes from upstream: joint1..7 renamed to panda_joint1..7 to match this
       project's naming convention everywhere else (pinn_controller_node.py's
       _JOINT_NAMES, pinocchio_baseline/panda.urdf). The upstream general/position
       actuators (actuator1..7) were REPLACED (not kept alongside) with a single
       direct-torque motor actuator per joint (gear=1, ctrlrange matching
       network/constants.TORQUE_LIMITS), see the <actuator> block's own comment
       for why: mujoco_ros2_control binds exactly one MuJoCo actuator per joint,
       so a position-servo actuator and a motor actuator can't coexist on the same
       joint the way an initial attempt here assumed. Both MoveIt2's default
       position-mode execution and the Stage 3 effort-mode path are backed by this
       one motor actuator; see panda_mujoco.ros2_control.xacro and
       config/mujoco_pid.yaml for how position control is achieved through it. -->
  <compiler angle="radian" meshdir="assets" autolimits="true"/>

  <option integrator="implicitfast" impratio="10"/>

  <default>
    <default class="panda">
      <material specular="0.5" shininess="0.25"/>
      <joint armature="0.1" damping="1" axis="0 0 1" range="-2.8973 2.8973"/>
      <general dyntype="none" biastype="affine" ctrlrange="-2.8973 2.8973" forcerange="-87 87"/>
      <default class="finger">
        <joint axis="0 1 0" type="slide" range="0 0.04"/>
      </default>

      <default class="panda/visual">
        <geom type="mesh" contype="0" conaffinity="0" group="2"/>
      </default>
      <default class="panda/collision">
        <geom type="mesh" group="3"/>
        <!-- Fingertip pad collision boxes, values as-is from google-deepmind/mujoco_menagerie's
             franka_emika_panda/panda.xml (the WITH-hand variant): a small set of boxes
             approximating the rubberized fingertip pad's actual contact patch, layered on top
             of the coarser finger_0 collision mesh below for stable, non-slip grasp contact. -->
        <default class="panda/fingertip_pad_collision_1">
          <geom type="box" size="0.0085 0.004 0.0085" pos="0 0.0055 0.0445"/>
        </default>
        <default class="panda/fingertip_pad_collision_2">
          <geom type="box" size="0.003 0.002 0.003" pos="0.0055 0.002 0.05"/>
        </default>
        <default class="panda/fingertip_pad_collision_3">
          <geom type="box" size="0.003 0.002 0.003" pos="-0.0055 0.002 0.05"/>
        </default>
        <default class="panda/fingertip_pad_collision_4">
          <geom type="box" size="0.003 0.002 0.0035" pos="0.0055 0.002 0.0395"/>
        </default>
        <default class="panda/fingertip_pad_collision_5">
          <geom type="box" size="0.003 0.002 0.0035" pos="-0.0055 0.002 0.0395"/>
